  "query_preview": "..\nIssued  CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nMonday through Saturday:\n\nA warm, humid, and active weather pattern is expected this\nupcoming week, following the progression of a warm front\nnorthward on Sunday and then a slow progression southward of a\nstationary/cold front Monday through the late week. With the\nfront present there will be daily chances for scattered showers\nand storms as weak waves propagate along the boundary. However,\nit is not expected to be a washout. Strong to severe storms may\noccur at times, especially midweek as better shear overlaps\nwith the frontal boundary.\n\nHeat and humidity are expected with highs near 90 Monday through\nWednesday and dewpoints in the low 70s. Temps may \"cool\" late-week\nas the front sags southward over the area, but \nshower/thunderstorm chances may continue into the beginning of\nnext weekend.\n\nCMiller",
